  "database": "rschema_0165",
  "nl_text": "The rschema_0165 database is a collection of tables that store information related to meteorological stations, operators, historical evolution information, and audit information. The Meteorological_Station table contains information about the physical location and characteristics of each station, including its elevation, geographic environment, latitude, longitude, observation elements, instrument name and model, observation record medium, observation standards, observation time, station ID, station name, and station type. The Operator table contains information about the people responsible for maintaining and operating the stations, including their name, email, phone number, role, and operator ID. The Historical_Evolution_Information table contains information about changes made to the station's information over time, including the change type, end time, new value, old value, operation status, operation time, reason for change, start time, station ID, and belonging station ID. The Audit_Information table contains information about the audit process, including the audit comments, audit status, audit time, change ID, operator ID, and primary key. The foreign keys in the tables ensure referential integrity, ensuring that the data in the tables is consistent and accurate.",
  "gold_question": "The meteorological information management system is designed to record and manage meteorological station information, historical evolution information, operator information, and audit records. Meteorological station information includes Station ID, Station Type (such as national station, regional station, marine station, sounding station, etc.), Station Name, Latitude, Longitude, Elevation, Geographic Environment Description, Observation Elements List, Observation Instrument Name and Model, Observation Time, Observation Record Medium, Observation Standards, and other relevant information. Historical evolution information includes Change ID, Station ID, Change Type (such as station name, station number, station location, observation elements, observation instruments, observation time, observation record medium, observation standards, etc.), Old Value, New Value, Start Time, End Time, Reason for Change, Operator ID, Operation Time, and Operation Status (such as pending selection, selected, historical data, etc.). Operator information includes Operator ID, Operator Name, Operator Level (such as provincial, city, county), Operator Role (such as system administrator, city and county user, etc.), Operator Email, and Operator Phone. Audit records include Change ID, Operator ID, Audit Time, Audit Status (such as approved, not approved), and Audit Comments. The system shall support operators in making changes to meteorological station information, recording historical evolutions, submitting audit requests, and auditors in reviewing change records and recording audit results. Each meteorological station can have multiple historical evolution records, each of which requires auditing, and each operator can submit multiple change records and participate in audits. The system shall be able to generate station change reports based on historical evolution information and record audit status and operators' operation history.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0165.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0165\nCREATE TABLE `meteorological_station` (\n  `station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `station_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `station_type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `latitude` decimal(9,6) NOT NULL,\n  `longitude` decimal(9,6) NOT NULL,\n  `elevation` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `geographic_environment` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_elements` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `instrument_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `instrument_model` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_record_medium` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_standards` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `observation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`station_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `operator` (\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`operator_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `historical_evolution_information` (\n  `change_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `belonging_station_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `change_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `old_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `new_value` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reason_for_change` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`change_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `historical_evolution_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`station_id`) REFERENCES `meteorological_station` (`station_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `historical_evolution_information_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`belonging_station_id`) REFERENCES `meteorological_station` (`station_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `audit_information` (\n  `audit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `change_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `operator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `audit_comments` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `audit_status` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `audit_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`audit_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `audit_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`change_id`) REFERENCES `historical_evolution_information` (`change_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `audit_information_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`operator_id`) REFERENCES `operator` (`operator_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
